            <ArticleTitle>[Health effects of indoor molds].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>462-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Molds are found almost everywhere in the environment. Their airborne propagules (conidia, spores, hyphal fragments) can--under certain circumstances--cause a variety of health problems like mycotic infections, allergies, asthma, irritations or toxic syndromes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
